From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:29:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s800x: Give the A9 iPhones' charger the
 USB host's grant

The A9 iPhones' SN2400 charger runs the iPhone 7 charging policy, whose
input foldback ramps towards the 2 A of the ADT usb-input-limit-max
until VBUS droops. The USB device controller names no supply, so on a
computer port nothing caps that ramp at what the host allows.

Give usbdev usb-psy-name, so the charger follows the host's grant
(100 mA unconfigured, then bMaxPower, more after an Apple host's
grant), and give serial5, the gauge's HDQ UART, a fixed alias as on
the iPad 5.

On the iPhone 6s Plus (2026-11-23) the gauge reads over HDQ through the
SN2400 switch, and from a Mac port the charger runs at the 500 mA grant
(0x09 = 0x29) and the battery charges at +250 mA net.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
index ac41c8e40..a6baf77a7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ aliases {
 		als0 = &als;	/* the loader copies the ADT's alsCalibration here */
 		spi2 = &spi2;
 		touchscreen0 = &touchscreen;	/* the loader copies the ADT calibration */
+		serial5 = &serial5;	/* the gauge's HDQ UART: a fixed port, as on the iPad 5 */
 	};
 };
 
@@ -175,3 +176,8 @@ &aop_gyro {
 		       "0", "1", "0",
 		       "0", "0", "1";
 };
+
+/* The USB device controller tells the SN2400 driver what the USB host allows. */
+&usbdev {
+	usb-psy-name = "usb";
+};
